commit 16f27a8653c71d3fba4019f719b6505a1d5c759f
Author: María <mariagrandury@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 16:36:20 2026 +0200

    pretrain: open the 3B rung at L30 and L50; document the outcomes
    
    The trained 3B 2x2 (A/B at L8/L15) yields only 2 mono-axis pairs on `L` and
    2 on `list` against a MIN_PAIRS of 3, so NO design axis is reportable at the
    3B reference and rq10 cannot answer its own question. That is a property of
    the 2x2's shape, not of the data. A-L30 + B-L30 take `L` to 6 and `list` to
    3 -- the minimum that clears both -- and A-L50 takes `L` to 9.
    
    SIZE_LANG_SETTINGS["3B"] gains 30 and 50, which is what makes
    fineweb_target_tokens size those builds at 165B rather than 92B (the target
    is derived from the grid's largest rung). AT3 gains an explicit 50: "1.7B"
    cap: it was capped at the reference for L15 and L30 but not L50, so opening
    that setting would otherwise have created an AT3 3B cell nobody planned.
    REBUILD_165 gains A:30 B:30 A:50; a T=1 allocation is proportional, so at a
    165B target every language draws ~47% of its own capacity and none is
    exhausted (A-L30 353.6B available, B-L30 341.4B, A-L50 373.7B).
    
    Grid 180 -> 183. No training launched: until the builds stage the three
    cells are refused by undersized_build (1.63 and 2.88 epochs), so registering
    them cannot start a 3B on repeated data by accident.
    
    build_status.sh: a stalled chain can also be one whose attempt budget is
    spent, and submit_build_one.sh refuses to queue a successor past
    BUILD_MAX_ATTEMPTS silently. The printed resubmit now counts the job's logs
    and carries the raised cap when it is needed -- FWEB lost a week to this,
    its 25 attempts burned by a corrupt-parquet loop in one evening.
    
    plan/90M-rung-anomaly.md records the retrain outcome: 56/58 cells, none
    diverged, the grid runs reproducing the diagnostics (2.719 against a
    predicted 2.715; 2.567 against 2.565), and the ladder residual at 175M going
    from +0.255 to -0.089. plan/l1_third_family.md records that DCLMP's +0.11
    training-loss gap is an entropy difference between corpora and not a quality
    one: on identical held-out documents the gap is 15x smaller, and on macro
    BPB DCLMP is better from 350M up.

